    "accepted_asymmetry": "Two tools return `accepted` under the same `unknown_diet` code and the lists DIFFER, on purpose. `describe_diet` and the REST routes serve the CATALOG (22 ids): the excluded entries have no principle card to return. `update_dietary_profile` serves the full VOCABULARY (26 ids): you can declare halal or gluten-free on your profile even though you cannot ask the catalog about them. A client must read `accepted` from the response it actually received rather than caching one list for both.",
